<p>Neutral voting for now.</p>
<p>I wholeheartedly approve of the legal and ethical ramifications explored by the Foundation, but I strongly dislike the doctor's note in the second collapsible. The point comes across damn well without it; it's like you don't trust your own writing to convey the message or the readers to understand it.</p>
<p>The second collapsible&#8230; I'm not sure how I feel about it. At first glance it's near-identical to the 'hidden' documentation in <a href="/scp-2950">SCP-2950</a> (especially because 11 was also the O5 in 2950) or <a href="/scp-1173">SCP-1173</a>, but I also kind of like the idea of the Foundation actively enabling defectors for the eventual usage of 2411 as a contingency plan.</p>

							</div>

								
