			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2577048">
									

<p>You may like it, but I would like to question on the strength of how it is used here. As a whole, it seems to be a simplistic cover that is clearly not the full story. It does not necessarily have a real reason to be there. I would regard the cover story to be on par with the low-level iterations of SCP-2317, which is blatantly an exercise in escalating clearance levels.</p>
<p>This article here does not do much with its cover. Hence, I do not feel that much would be lost if the cover is not known in the article. Perhaps that is indeed a Level 1 version, for people who don't know&#8230; but this layer has little relevance and I feel that the hook is not optimised by having pushed into a collapsible.</p>
<p>Overall, brevity is the soul of wit. I guess the excess is a garnish that is ultimately artificial since most readers of SCPs can garner that &quot;There is a collapsible noting high clearance levels; that should be the real meat of the article.&quot;</p>

